1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,950
Esports World Cup 2026 Takes Paris.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:15,475
The Esports World Cup 2026 descends on Paris this summer, featuring a record-breaking $75 million prize pool and over 2,000 competitors from more than 80 countries.

3
00:00:15,475 --> 00:00:28,200
The event, running across multiple venues in the French capital, spans two full weeks of competition across 20 titles including League of Legends, Counter-Strike 2, Valorant, and Street Fighter 6.

4
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:35,987
Organizers report that ticket sales have exceeded 300,000, with millions more watching via streaming platforms.

5
00:00:35,987 --> 00:00:42,662
The Paris games mark the second edition of the tournament, which was first held in Riyadh in 2024.

6
00:00:42,662 --> 00:00:53,700
Viewership is expected to surpass last year's record of 500 million unique online viewers, cementing the Esports World Cup as the largest competitive gaming event in history.

7
00:00:53,700 --> 00:01:03,650
The event has drawn sponsorships from major global brands, and Paris officials have touted the tournament as a milestone for esports legitimacy on the international stage.

